WEBVTT

00:22.040 --> 00:23.680
<i>ONE MORE TIME</i>

00:23.880 --> 00:28.630
I LOOKED AT THE BLOOMING
FLOWERS IN MY SHINING DREAM

00:28.800 --> 00:32.350
<i>NO MORE LIFE</i>
I WAS OBSESSED

00:32.520 --> 00:35.110
MY PAST WAS SCATTERED

00:35.280 --> 00:38.670
<i>JEALOUS</i>, <i>JEALOUS</i>
BY THOSE HANDS

00:38.840 --> 00:41.990
<i>JEALOUS</i>, <i>JEALOUS</i>
I WAS CALLED

00:42.160 --> 00:45.310
<i>JEALOUS</i>, <i>JEALOUS</i>
BY A LIGHT SHINING

00:45.480 --> 00:48.710
<i>JEALOUS</i>, <i>JEALOUS</i>
IN THE DARKNESS

00:48.880 --> 00:52.320
<i>ONE MORE TIME</i>
IN THE TWINKLING LIGHT

00:52.480 --> 00:55.440
WATCH THAT FIGURE FADE AWAY

00:55.600 --> 00:59.230
<i>NO MORE LIFE</i>
I WAS LEFT BEHIND

00:59.400 --> 01:02.150
BUT TOMORROW WE'LL MEET AGAIN

01:02.320 --> 01:05.440
<i>JEALOUS</i>, <i>JEALOUS</i>
BY THOSE HANDS

01:05.600 --> 01:08.750
<i>JEALOUS</i>, <i>JEALOUS</i>
I WAS CALLED

01:08.920 --> 01:12.150
<i>JEALOUS</i>, <i>JEALOUS</i>
BY A LIGHT SHINING

01:12.320 --> 01:15.470
<i>JEALOUS</i>, <i>JEALOUS</i>
IN THE DARKNESS

01:15.640 --> 01:21.400
SURROUNDED BY THE LIGHT

01:21.560 --> 01:23.840
<i>DON'T CLOSE EYES
HELP ME</i>

01:24.000 --> 01:29.330
WHEN I SCREAM
<i>WILL BE SATISFACTION, YOU KNOW</i>

01:32.820 --> 01:37.040
The seventh month of 1600 AD, or Keicho 5.

01:37.410 --> 01:41.210
Charging Tokugawa Ieyasu with thirteen articles of impeachment,

01:41.210 --> 01:48.130
Ishida Mitsunari sent messengers to various daimyo in the name of the Toyotomi clan,

01:48.130 --> 01:51.300
telling them to raise armies.

01:51.300 --> 01:56.390
At the same time, beings seeking to end the period of turbulence

01:56.390 --> 02:00.270
and build a kingdom to last a thousand years

02:00.270 --> 02:04.520
were about to awaken from a thousand-year sleep.

02:04.520 --> 02:06.520
And then...

02:06.520 --> 02:10.280
On the fifteenth day of the ninth month, at Sekigahara,

02:10.280 --> 02:12.740
the Eastern Army of Tokugawa Ieyasu clashed with

02:12.740 --> 02:17.870
the Western Army of the Toyotomi clan and Ishida Mitsunari.

02:17.870 --> 02:21.330
As a result of the performance of Kobayakawa Hideaki's troops,

02:21.330 --> 02:27.250
the Western Army of the Toyotomi clan and
Ishida Mitsunari achieved a sweeping victory,

02:27.250 --> 02:33.510
bringing what should have been
three hundred years of peace to the world.

02:34.340 --> 02:39.390
You should all be quite familiar with this story...

02:46.080 --> 02:47.880
My name is Desperado...

02:48.320 --> 02:50.990
I am a <i>femme fatale</i>
from a far away land.

02:51.560 --> 02:55.830
I didn't show up for a
long time, but I saw...

02:56.560 --> 03:00.520
that a new heroine named Yume
was accompanying Musashi.

03:00.680 --> 03:03.800
I thought I was the heroine of the series!

03:04.440 --> 03:07.110
I am not okay with this at all!

03:07.280 --> 03:10.590
No more English humor.

03:11.120 --> 03:16.670
To find the second artifact,
we have infiltrated a castle.

03:17.480 --> 03:20.760
But then I found myself facing
my alter ego from the past!

03:20.920 --> 03:23.120
Is this magic?

03:23.280 --> 03:26.750
Japanese Yin-Yang monks
are very, very strong!

03:26.920 --> 03:31.550
And if I don't kill my past self,
I'll be stuck in the castle!

03:31.720 --> 03:38.950
With all these contradictions,
it's total panic in my head!

03:47.220 --> 03:50.070
RIDDLE SORCERER

03:55.880 --> 03:57.550
Well then?

03:57.720 --> 04:00.190
Don't you want to get out of here?

04:00.360 --> 04:01.840
I do!

04:02.280 --> 04:05.880
You want to find the treasure
hidden in this castle!

04:06.040 --> 04:07.240
Exactly!

04:07.560 --> 04:09.710
Then you just have to kill me.

04:10.200 --> 04:13.510
You're stronger than me,
it should be easy!

04:14.080 --> 04:18.520
Why should I kill my past self?

04:22.760 --> 04:26.920
Are you saying that if I don't
kill you, I can't get out?

04:27.520 --> 04:28.720
Exactly.

04:34.880 --> 04:41.160
But if you kill your past self,
you will disappear!

04:41.800 --> 04:43.150
This is a paradox!

04:44.800 --> 04:46.840
This is a contradiction.

04:47.080 --> 04:48.280
Yeah.

04:50.560 --> 04:53.280
So I'm stuck here?

04:53.840 --> 04:55.040
Yeah.

05:00.480 --> 05:03.150
Is there really no other way?

05:09.760 --> 05:12.800
I was really classy when I was young!

05:13.360 --> 05:17.320
I was even more handsome when I was alive.

05:19.640 --> 05:21.440
Horrible monster!

05:22.280 --> 05:25.750
I'm suffering too, don't be so mean!

05:26.200 --> 05:28.350
Who are you?

05:28.520 --> 05:31.750
Only our future selves are
supposed to come here.

05:32.440 --> 05:35.480
I am indeed what you become in the future.

05:35.640 --> 05:39.520
The lord of the land of Kai, <i>Minamoto
no Harunobu</i>, Shingen Takeda!

05:40.120 --> 05:42.560
Enough of your jokes!

05:42.720 --> 05:47.840
I am a determined, brave and manly man!

05:48.000 --> 05:50.990
I can't become this doughy monster!

05:51.560 --> 05:55.520
I understand your doubts, but it is reality.

05:55.880 --> 05:59.510
Are you really my future self?

06:04.960 --> 06:07.760
And I am Ieyasu Tokugawa in the future.

06:10.520 --> 06:14.510
Has history turned all warlords into monsters?

06:15.040 --> 06:17.270
Not quite.

06:17.720 --> 06:21.190
We have transformed due to certain circumstances.

06:21.680 --> 06:25.720
It sounds crazy, but believe us.

06:30.000 --> 06:33.040
Don't make that face, please!

06:36.400 --> 06:40.840
Don't worry, we won't do anything to you!

06:41.560 --> 06:45.470
I just wanted to see myself younger.

06:46.360 --> 06:49.670
I just came here for nostalgia.

06:49.840 --> 06:51.040
Don't worry!

07:04.680 --> 07:07.190
Bastard, what are you doing?

07:07.480 --> 07:08.910
That's obvious!

07:09.440 --> 07:11.220
Are you gonna commit <i>seppuku</i>?

07:11.400 --> 07:18.320
Future Shingen, future Ieyasu, didn't you
know that once you entered this room,

07:18.480 --> 07:21.790
you couldn't get out
without killing us?

07:22.480 --> 07:26.100
- I didn't know! Did you?
- No!

07:26.120 --> 07:31.430
But if you kill your past self,
your current self will disappear.

07:31.600 --> 07:33.430
That's how the castle was made.

07:33.960 --> 07:44.230
But Shingen and I decided to kill ourselves rather
than let you kill us, to make you disappear!

07:45.160 --> 07:46.360
Why?

07:47.400 --> 07:48.990
The reason is simple.

07:49.480 --> 07:55.070
We don't want to live if we're gonna
turn into the monsters in front of us!

07:55.280 --> 07:57.030
It is natural for a samurai!

07:58.120 --> 07:59.600
Wait a minute!

07:59.760 --> 08:03.150
Shingen will certainly die of stomach cancer.

08:03.320 --> 08:08.240
Butt for my dear past self,
a long life awaits you!

08:08.400 --> 08:09.600
Do not die!

08:10.160 --> 08:11.960
Am I going to die of cancer?

08:12.200 --> 08:14.350
Actually, yes.

08:14.680 --> 08:15.880
Cancer?

08:16.200 --> 08:18.320
Why did you tell him that?

08:19.320 --> 08:20.990
I beg your pardon!

08:21.160 --> 08:24.040
- Don't kill yourself!
- That's right!

08:24.480 --> 08:26.990
Do not die!
Say no to suicide!

08:28.520 --> 08:30.750
Don't run away, my dear future me!

08:31.200 --> 08:38.030
But what was the crazy guy
who set up this trap thinking?

08:41.240 --> 08:43.040
Do something!

08:43.200 --> 08:45.640
I'm in a panic!

08:46.480 --> 08:52.460
If a Yin-Yang monk created this
trap, there must be an exit!

08:52.480 --> 08:56.630
So, find it, do something!

09:00.440 --> 09:07.230
If I get out of this, I'll have some words
for the monk who created this trap!

09:08.040 --> 09:10.190
Only if you get out!

09:10.800 --> 09:13.030
I can't take it!

09:13.200 --> 09:15.840
I'm going to be locked up in here all my life!

09:16.440 --> 09:20.520
Not exactly, you'll die in here!

09:22.840 --> 09:26.120
OSAKA

09:32.160 --> 09:35.310
Princess Kaguya, is this horse suitable for you?

09:38.240 --> 09:40.750
I do like it. I'll take it.

09:46.800 --> 09:49.680
Lord Sarutobi, do you really not need a horse?

09:50.800 --> 09:53.390
A ninja runs faster than a horse.

09:54.520 --> 10:03.150
According to Dabinoji's map, the
third artifact is located on the far west.

10:04.560 --> 10:07.160
We'll get there the day
after tomorrow if we trot.

10:18.780 --> 10:22.240
EDO

10:37.240 --> 10:42.680
How can a stone imprison the ayakashi?

10:48.040 --> 10:51.720
At first glance, it looks
like an ordinary lens.

10:56.120 --> 11:00.350
It's probably worth looking into it a bit more.

11:19.400 --> 11:20.600
What is this?

11:41.280 --> 11:42.790
Who are you?

11:43.720 --> 11:45.230
A Yin-Yang monk.

11:46.120 --> 11:47.320
Your name?

11:47.840 --> 11:49.190
Urashima.

11:49.640 --> 11:52.900
- Urashima? Taro Urashima?
- Yes.

11:52.920 --> 11:56.150
I don't know a monk named Urashima.

11:56.920 --> 12:00.960
I only know the monk Haruaki Abe.

12:03.640 --> 12:05.150
You don't smell anything?

12:05.600 --> 12:06.800
I do.

12:08.880 --> 12:12.080
That's because I ate a
garlic pizza this morning.

12:12.600 --> 12:14.670
It smells like ayakashi.

12:15.120 --> 12:16.520
Obviously.…

12:16.680 --> 12:19.880
This is the basement of an ayakashi's castle.

12:20.600 --> 12:25.120
Does this mean that an artifact
is in the hands of an ayakashi?

12:25.880 --> 12:29.080
Only one for now.

12:31.400 --> 12:33.440
You look surprised.

12:34.200 --> 12:40.430
I set traps in each of the castles
where the artifacts are located.

12:41.480 --> 12:44.230
It was a human who retrieved it.

12:44.400 --> 12:47.040
The ayakashi just took it away from him.

12:49.520 --> 12:53.960
So, you've set all these traps?

12:54.120 --> 12:57.960
- Yes.
- They seem to be very advanced.

13:01.680 --> 13:05.880
Doesn't it bother you that
these artifacts may get stolen?

13:06.040 --> 13:08.950
I don't exist materially at the moment.

13:09.640 --> 13:12.760
So I can't get the artifacts.

13:13.160 --> 13:14.460
Nevertheless...

13:14.680 --> 13:20.870
I can help these humans to prevent the
ayakashi from taking the other artifacts.

13:21.280 --> 13:25.350
Hold on. Let me ask you a question before you go.

13:25.520 --> 13:27.830
I will answer only one question.

13:28.440 --> 13:29.840
That's fine with me.

13:30.440 --> 13:31.790
I'm listening.

13:32.160 --> 13:34.670
Where are you really?

13:35.240 --> 13:39.760
Are you no longer in this world?

13:40.120 --> 13:42.400
I am...

13:43.000 --> 13:44.230
elsewhere.

13:44.400 --> 13:47.790
But I'm not me anymore.

13:48.320 --> 13:49.520
I understand.

13:53.000 --> 13:55.230
You remind me of someone.

13:58.200 --> 14:02.560
And the way you run away
reminds me very much of him.

14:14.560 --> 14:17.280
There is no anti-ayakashi barrier.

14:17.440 --> 14:22.430
This Yin-Yang monk seems
to be confident in his traps.

14:24.000 --> 14:30.520
I'm going to watch as a sole
spectator to see how Musashi does.

14:50.520 --> 14:52.590
Is everything okay, Princess Kaguya?

14:57.960 --> 14:59.840
The princess is fine.

15:00.440 --> 15:02.800
I'm glad to hear that.

15:03.600 --> 15:05.240
Any ayakashi there?

15:05.400 --> 15:08.760
No, I don't feel their presence.

15:09.760 --> 15:11.560
But it's not from our world.

15:12.000 --> 15:16.470
If it is foreign to our world,
is it a specter, a ghost?

15:16.640 --> 15:23.190
As long as I'm alive,
I won't let it even touch you!

15:23.880 --> 15:26.000
That's easy to say.

15:31.600 --> 15:32.800
Who are you?

15:33.400 --> 15:35.070
The monk Yin-Yang Urashima.

15:35.280 --> 15:36.480
Urashima?

15:37.080 --> 15:38.830
A Yin-Yang monk?

15:39.000 --> 15:41.670
Like the one who hid the artifacts?

15:42.360 --> 15:46.120
If you want to find these
artifacts, I will help you.

15:46.520 --> 15:49.720
Bastard, what are you planing?

15:52.680 --> 15:54.670
Princess Kaguya, be careful!

16:06.280 --> 16:07.790
Everything is fine.

16:07.960 --> 16:11.560
Urashima, I thank you for your proposal.

16:12.120 --> 16:14.030
Princess Kaguya!

16:16.720 --> 16:21.600
Urashima, how do you plan to help us?

16:22.680 --> 16:28.080
I will transport you immediately
to the castle where you are going.

16:28.240 --> 16:29.800
Is this even possible?

16:30.560 --> 16:32.790
Yes, with the art of Yin-Yang.

16:34.680 --> 16:36.990
I thank you for your help.

16:37.160 --> 16:38.430
Princess Kaguya!

16:39.880 --> 16:43.870
Danjo, this person seems to be trustworthy.

16:44.200 --> 16:47.240
If Princess Kaguya says so...

16:47.400 --> 16:55.360
But if you are so powerful, can't you do
anything about the traps in the castles?

16:55.840 --> 16:57.350
That's impossible.

16:57.840 --> 16:59.040
That's selfish!

16:59.440 --> 17:01.400
Well, let's go.

17:07.400 --> 17:12.280
YAMAGUCHI'S

17:07.400 --> 17:12.280
AKIYOSHIDO CAVE

17:20.520 --> 17:21.720
Where are we?

17:21.760 --> 17:24.400
It looks like a stalactite cave.

17:24.600 --> 17:25.800
Goodbye.

17:27.680 --> 17:29.080
He disappeared.

17:29.240 --> 17:33.360
It looked like Yasha's teleportation.

17:33.520 --> 17:38.240
Yes, this man looks quite like Yasha.

17:38.600 --> 17:39.870
Princess Kaguya!

17:40.640 --> 17:41.840
Come see this!

17:43.560 --> 17:45.560
It's a castle!
A castle!

17:56.840 --> 18:00.150
- There's a castle down there.
- Hiding an artifact.

18:07.640 --> 18:11.840
Wait! If you die, what happens to
your dream of unifying the country?

18:12.600 --> 18:15.040
Have you succeeded in unifying the country?

18:15.240 --> 18:16.720
No, actually...

18:17.120 --> 18:20.750
You can die whenever you want!

18:20.920 --> 18:26.030
Besides, you're still young, you
still have a lot of scores to settle.

18:26.200 --> 18:28.590
Can you ignore them?

18:29.560 --> 18:32.550
Have you finished the war
against Kenshin Uesugi?

18:33.000 --> 18:34.200
Oops!

18:34.920 --> 18:37.990
Who has defeated in Kanawakajima?

18:40.680 --> 18:41.880
Did you lose?

18:41.920 --> 18:44.510
- I didn't lose!
- Then you won!

18:45.240 --> 18:46.720
Not exactly...

18:47.520 --> 18:51.400
What a miserable future! I'd rather die!

18:51.800 --> 18:53.000
Me too!

18:53.080 --> 18:54.310
Wait!

18:56.480 --> 18:58.840
You usurper from the future!

19:00.760 --> 19:02.510
You'll pay with your life!

19:02.720 --> 19:05.950
I'm not an impostor! Help me!

19:06.520 --> 19:10.310
If you're a real ninja,
don't beg for mercy!

19:10.480 --> 19:12.840
- That's shameful!
- But...

19:13.040 --> 19:14.240
Die!

19:20.320 --> 19:21.640
I am alive...

19:22.360 --> 19:23.560
And...

19:27.040 --> 19:28.550
I am out...

19:34.160 --> 19:35.590
It never ends.

19:36.160 --> 19:37.910
How long will it last?

19:38.240 --> 19:39.440
Yeah.

19:39.880 --> 19:42.870
Let your past self kill you.

19:44.320 --> 19:46.790
Who just spoke?

19:48.440 --> 19:53.040
There is no other way out
of this infernal paradox.

19:56.320 --> 19:58.990
Who said that?
Did you hear it?

19:59.160 --> 20:01.230
Yes, very clearly.

20:01.840 --> 20:03.880
But I can't do that!

20:04.040 --> 20:05.710
Death is the end!

20:05.880 --> 20:08.630
Maybe that is the answer.

20:08.960 --> 20:10.160
The answer?

20:10.240 --> 20:13.520
The past is a road already traveled.

20:13.680 --> 20:15.030
There is only one.

20:15.200 --> 20:18.490
On the other hand, the future
is an infinity of possibilities.

20:19.960 --> 20:25.990
Even if your past self kills you, it will
not necessarily destroy your future.

20:26.640 --> 20:30.710
It may guide you to a different path.

20:31.320 --> 20:33.150
That is a possible interpretation.

20:33.840 --> 20:37.040
I don't really understand
what you're saying, too bad.

20:39.280 --> 20:40.480
Make it quick!

20:41.120 --> 20:43.270
You finally gave up.

20:51.760 --> 20:56.870
I don't know who said that,
but maybe I should listen.

21:00.200 --> 21:01.430
Get ready!

21:10.080 --> 21:16.870
I wouldn't like to be killed by someone else, but if it's by myself, go ahead.

21:28.520 --> 21:30.590
- We are alive.
- Yes.

21:30.760 --> 21:31.960
You too...

21:32.120 --> 21:33.320
You were able to leave.

21:33.640 --> 21:34.840
Yes.

21:34.920 --> 21:37.590
- The voice was telling the truth.
- Yes.

21:37.960 --> 21:40.680
Master Musashi!
Everyone!

21:43.360 --> 21:45.870
You're safe too, Ninjataro!

21:47.880 --> 21:49.920
Ninjataro, it can't be!

21:51.720 --> 21:52.920
Well, it can!

21:55.200 --> 21:57.790
- The artifact!
- Did you find it?

21:58.280 --> 22:00.080
Yes! Are you impressed?

22:00.200 --> 22:04.440
- Amazing.
- Yeah. How did you do it?

22:05.120 --> 22:13.150
Sorry? I just listened a strange voice in
my heart that guided me to the artifact.

22:15.600 --> 22:17.560
That voice again?

22:17.920 --> 22:20.150
Yes. Do you know who it was?

22:20.800 --> 22:24.350
No, but it sounded familiar.

22:25.000 --> 22:26.200
Familiar?

22:26.680 --> 22:30.470
I think I've heard it somewhere before.

22:30.640 --> 22:32.550
Familiar and sad at the same time.

22:34.080 --> 22:38.710
The second artifact must not
fall into the hands of ayakashi!

22:39.480 --> 22:43.000
It seems that they got the second artifact.

22:56.000 --> 22:59.150
What is this headache?

22:59.600 --> 23:00.920
It hurts...

23:11.400 --> 23:15.870
I have to give up on the
second artifact for now.

23:21.000 --> 23:24.040
Yasha. So it was him...

23:25.840 --> 23:28.280
So please, don't die!

23:28.480 --> 23:29.680
I will!

23:30.120 --> 23:31.760
- Me too!
- No!

23:32.680 --> 23:35.750
I feel like this is going to take a while...

23:39.280 --> 23:43.880
I don't know whose voice that was, but thanks!

23:44.720 --> 23:46.070
Let's go!

23:46.560 --> 23:50.950
Let's go find the third artifact!

24:23.440 --> 24:25.190
MAKE HASTE

24:25.360 --> 24:27.160
THROUGH THE CROWDS

24:27.320 --> 24:31.080
THEY'RE CUTTING OFF YOUR ESCAPE

24:31.240 --> 24:34.950
IN THIS TWILIGHT TOWN
I HEAR PIERCING SOUNDS

24:35.120 --> 24:38.880
LIKE A WANDERING CAT

24:39.040 --> 24:40.790
WITHOUT KNOWING

24:40.960 --> 24:42.760
WHERE TO GO

24:42.920 --> 24:46.680
I'M TRAPPED IN THIS TOWN THAT NEVER SLEEPS

24:46.840 --> 24:50.360
MY REFLECTION IN THE MIRROR

24:50.520 --> 24:55.200
SEEING MYSELF TRANSFORM

24:55.360 --> 24:57.720
I'M HOLDING ON

24:57.880 --> 25:01.160
FOR AS LONG AS POSSIBLE

25:03.200 --> 25:07.830
I'LL SHOW YOU THAT I CAN

25:08.000 --> 25:10.560
WIN OVER THIS TOWN

25:11.720 --> 25:13.760
FROM MY BURNING HEART

25:13.920 --> 25:15.910
SHINE SO MANY

25:20.040 --> 25:21.550
FLOODING ALL OVER

25:21.720 --> 25:23.710
SCATTERING ALL OVER

25:23.880 --> 25:27.030
SURROUNDING ME

25:27.200 --> 25:29.650
SOLEMNLY

25:31.040 --> 25:37.110
So, Yasha and this Yin-Yang
monk knew each other?

25:37.840 --> 25:40.070
Who is stronger?

25:40.560 --> 25:43.680
The next chapter: <i>Urashima and Yasha!</i>!
